course: dictionary
lesson: 11209
title: Wonder: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can do different jobs, and the words around it show which job it is doing. «I wonder why the sky turns orange at sunset» uses wonder for thinking: the speaker wants to know the answer. «The children stared in wonder at the glowing lights» uses wonder for a feeling: they were amazed.
explain: Look for the clues. Is wonder doing something, like wondering or wondered? Or is it a naming word, like a wonder or the wonders of the world? «Alice sits with her face in her hands, wondering if anything will ever happen» shows wondering as thinking, because she is turning a question over in her mind.
explain: «No wonder» is a useful phrase. «No wonder she is tired, she walked for ten miles» means it is not surprising that she is tired. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: if the sentence still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: Wonder can be a verb (wonder, wonders, wondered, wondering) or a noun (wonder, a wonder, wonders).
fact: To wonder means to think about something and want to know the answer.
fact: Wonder as a noun is a feeling of surprise and amazement at something beautiful or strange.
fact: «A wonder» means something amazing, such as the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.
fact: «No wonder» means it is not surprising. Polite requests also use «I wonder if you could…».
exercise: «I wonder why the sky turns orange at sunset.» What does wonder mean here? | To buy something cheap | *To think and want to know the answer | To be amazed by a dog | To fall asleep
exercise: «The children stared in wonder at the glowing lights.» What does «in wonder» show? | Anger at being woken early | *Amazement at something beautiful | Hunger after a long day | Boredom with the lights
exercise: «No wonder she is tired, she walked for ten miles.» What does «no wonder» mean here? | It is a prize for the winner | It is a secret that must be hidden | It is a surprise party for her | *It is not surprising
test: In «The Seven Wonders of the Ancient World are famous buildings», what kind of word is wonder? | A question word | A verb | *A noun | An adjective
test: Which sentence is a polite request? | Name the wonders of the world | *I wonder if you could pass the salt | Stare in wonder at the sea | No wonder you are late
exam: «Psalm 8 looks up at the moon and stars and wonders why God cares about small human beings.» What does wonders mean here? | Is amazed by a bright shiny thing | *Thinks about something and wants to know the answer | Counts the stars one by one | Hopes to win a prize
